        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(context-engine): add reference context channel",
        "body": "Closes #88753\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nContext-engine authors need a safe way to provide historical summaries, memories, or retrieved context without encoding that data as fresh user messages or higher-authority prompt additions. Without a dedicated lane, compacted/reference data can regain too much prompt authority or interfere with provider message constraints.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a narrow `AssembleResult.referenceContext` SDK lane plus a `reference-context` host capability. Embedded and Codex app-server hosts validate the shape, then render the items through host-owned lower-authority reference blocks instead of letting engines smuggle reference data into executable conversation history.\n\n## User Impact\n\nContext-engine and plugin developers can now return historical/reference data separately from model-history messages. Users get safer continuity because historical summaries are explicitly framed as quoted lower-authority context, not as a new user turn or new instruction.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/context-engine/reference-context.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/harness/context-engine-lifecycle.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/context-engine-projection.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.context-engine.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.src.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/test-src.tsbuildinfo`\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.extensions.test.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/extensions-test.tsbuildinfo`\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.plugin-sdk.dts.json --declaration true`",
